# Sample .worktreeinclude for the repository root. Project setup offers it with orca.yaml.
# One literal path per line, relative to the repository root; no wildcards, no negations.
# Orca copies the entries from the primary checkout into each new worktree, only when they exist and Git ignores them
# (a local setup lists them in .git/info/exclude).
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.override.md
.benchkeeper/state.json
skills-lock.json
.claude/skills
.agents/skills
